-- erwartet: E001
-- **The stumm edge, pinned (`H021`).** `stumm` is an `extern fn` with NO `effects`
-- clause: the declaration falls with `E001`, and that verdict carries this file.
--
-- But the CALLER's edge draws nothing of its own. The derivation finds no body and
-- no line to derive from (`stumm` bookkeeping), drops the edge into a lower bound
-- (`unvollstaendig`), and an `E009` hint is all that names the call. A derivation
-- that cannot resolve a target must refuse AT THE CALLER -- that refusal is `H021`
-- (assigned, verified free; the rule stands ready in `ableitung.rs`, unwired:
-- central assembly is frozen for this lane -- see `messung/ABLEITUNG-WEG.md`).
--
-- The twin (`ruft_rand`) calls the same shape WITH a declared line: the edge of the
-- checked world (`Rand`), silent by design -- `H021` must never touch it. This file
-- must fall with `E001` and nothing else at `Fehler` level: that single code is what
-- proves the call itself silent.
module gift::stumm_edge_pinned {

-- No `effects`: the declaration falls with `E001`.
extern fn stumm() costs <= 2 ops;

-- The edge of the checked world: no body, but a declared line. Silent by design.
extern fn rand() effects { pure } costs <= 2 ops;

-- Must stay silent at `Fehler` level: the edge to `stumm` draws no refusal of its
-- own today (an `E009` hint at most). `H021` would fall here, once, at the caller.
impl fn ruft_stumm() effects { pure } costs <= 8 ops
{
    stumm();
}

-- Must stay silent in every world: `Rand`, not a hole.
impl fn ruft_rand() effects { pure } costs <= 8 ops
{
    rand();
}

}
